In article <3073@ohm.sw.mcc.com> daneman@ohm.sw.mcc.com (Michael Daneman) writes:
>If you use a blessed enchant srcoll on an uncursed object, the object first
>gets blessed (which uses up +1 I guess) and then enchanted to +2.  If you
>use it on a cursed object it will, I think, bless it and enchant it to +1.
>If you use it on a blessed object, then it will enchant it to +3.  This
>is not completely accurate, but it's pretty close to the truth.

I just tried this in explore mode.  Blessed scrolls of enchant weapon always
increase the plus of the weapon by 3 unless the weapon gets over enchanted.

As for the cursed/blessed status of the weapons, the first scroll I used
uncursed the weapon in addition to adding +3 to the enchantment.  Subsequent
scrolls did not change the cursed/uncursed/blessed status of the weapon for
some reason.  I do not know why; I expected each scroll to modify the the
status by one level upwards.  Thus, starting with a cursed +1 war hammer,
two blessed scrolls of enchant weapon made a +7 war hammer which was uncursed.

Blessed scrolls of enchant armor are different than enchant weapon.  They
modify the enchantment by +1, +2, or +3 depending on a random factor.  I
assume they work similar to blessed enchant weapon scrolls wrt cursed/blessed
status.

Anyone know why the war hammer I tested never got blessed?
